<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ram Singh I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1688">1688</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Ram Singh I of Amber</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ram Singh I was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kachhwaha">Kachhwaha</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> ruler of Amber from 1667 to 1688 and a general of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aurangzeb">Aurangzeb</a> sent him to reconquer the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmaputra">Brahmaputra</a> valley from the Ahom kingdom, and in 1671 his army and fleet were defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lachit-borphukan">Lachit Borphukan</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-saraighat">Battle of Saraighat</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guwahati">Guwahati</a>. Earlier he had been responsible for the custody of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivaji">Shivaji</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agra">Agra</a>, from where the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> leader escaped in 1666.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ram-singh-i.jpg" alt="Ram Singh I" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Indian, North India, Mughal (Shah Jahan Period) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ram_Singh_of_Amber.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
